    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52f538a5_4c8812b3",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T05:16:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well.. I don\u0027t think this code makes microdroid_manager involved in any communications. microdroid_manager just redirects payload\u0027s output, and I see no differences between this and the old implementation that microdroid_manager passes a FD for payload output.\n\nWhat I mean \"involved\" is that microdroid_manager can\u0027t affect direct communcations between apps.",
      "parentUuid": "239265c3_b3ec1fee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd3f97b2_607f229d",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T05:22:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously, microdroid_manager didn\u0027t play a role once the FD was passed to the apps. Now, it is responsible for relaying the bits, causing unnecessary context switches for every communication between the apps.",
      "parentUuid": "52f538a5_4c8812b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f70d324_8f941736",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T05:37:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, it makes sense. However, if we want to remove such context switches, we really need to do one of the followings:\n\n1) A guest VM makes three connections with the virtualization service: VirtualMachineService, stdout, stderr. I think this is against our decision.\n2) The RPC vsock connection supports passing a file descriptor, which is not supported yet.\n3) We give up handling payload outputs. (Seems like a bad idea though!)\n4) Each payload opens its own output server. This would be fine, but we still need context switches within the app, because we don\u0027t wait for the connection to output server forever.\n\nWill there be any better ideas?",
      "parentUuid": "fd3f97b2_607f229d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f38a95f0_17468320",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T05:53:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think this is against our decision\n\nWe haven\u0027t made any new decision about how to pass stdin/out/err across the apps.\n\n\u003e supports passing a file descriptor\n\nThe FD should be backed by a regular file. So we wouldn\u0027t be able to rely on that for sharing stdin/out/err.",
      "parentUuid": "9f70d324_8f941736",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "77ebbccc_50cd972b",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T06:13:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We haven\u0027t made any new decision about how to pass stdin/out/err across the apps.\n\nWhat I mean here is that the guest VM connects only once (for the binder connection); we don\u0027t want to make more connections, right?\n\nOne suggestion: how about this?\n\n1) the payload fully initializes the vm, and then returns.\n2) microdroid manager waits until the payload is finished.\n3) microdroid manager passes the payload\u0027s output (as a string) to the virtualization service via a parameter of onPayloadFinished() method. (renamed from onPayloadStarted)",
      "parentUuid": "f38a95f0_17468320",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29fdb496_c6c67bef",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T06:19:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To support stdin and stderr in addition to stdout, we need more connections.\n\n\u003e microdroid manager waits until the payload is finished.\n\nThis doesn\u0027t work if the payload runs for a long time, or never stops. The reason we need stdout/stderr from the app is to see any output from the app \"in real-time\".",
      "parentUuid": "77ebbccc_50cd972b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fa50c08_4d64eb28",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T06:25:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The reason we need stdout/stderr from the app is to see any output from the app \"in real-time\".\n\nokay.\n\n\u003e To support stdin and stderr in addition to stdout, we need more connections.\n\nOkay. It\u0027s fine to have more connections. However, what I don\u0027t like is that the virtualization service opens a server (...which is done by handle_connection_from_vm() so far), and the guest VM has to connect to the server.",
      "parentUuid": "29fdb496_c6c67bef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
