      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T06:32:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is wrong with VS listening on a port?",
      "parentUuid": "9fa50c08_4d64eb28",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "021e8237_fcfb7bd4",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T06:48:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not \"wrong\". I just don\u0027t like it. Especially, we can\u0027t get rid of handle_connection_from_vm() function, and virtualization service becomes complicated (because we now have to store 3 file descriptors per VM inside virtualization service).\n\nFor me, the additional context switching doesn\u0027t seem to be too expensive. Usually we\u0027ll only need stdout, and I think it\u0027s more reasonable for the VM to host an output server, because it\u0027s the VM that controls the data. Isn\u0027t it expensive too, when we have to make three more connections every time? The connection itself involves many context switching.",
      "parentUuid": "522939c7_884c8823",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "426d793f_476ba79d",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T07:07:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, but \"I don\u0027t like it\" can\u0027t be a reason for a design. You don\u0027t need to permanently keep the file descriptors inside VS. Once they are passed to the client, they can be freed.\n\nThe overhead for creating three connections is paid only once when the payload is started, whereas the overhead for relaying the streams is paid every time when there\u0027s something to send or receive.\n\nIf you are still concerned about having three connections, you could optimize it by sharing a single connection for in and out because a socket connection is full duplex. stderr could be merged into stdout (or just ignored) based on the configuration that the app has specified.",
      "parentUuid": "021e8237_fcfb7bd4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 98
      },
      "revId": "072bcd8eac7d0bc8d9e32a6610308c0f9630f175",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "85b62802_d89450e1",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291338
