      "writtenOn": "2021-08-23T07:15:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Sorry, but \"I don\u0027t like it\" can\u0027t be a reason for a design. \n\nNo need to be sorry at all.\n\n\u003e If you are still concerned about having three connections, you could optimize it by sharing a single connection for in and out because a socket connection is full duplex. stderr could be merged into stdout (or just ignored) based on the configuration that the app has specified.\n\nThis sounds reasonable. I\u0027ll work this way.",
      "parentUuid": "426d793f_476ba79d",
